<p>Early Gen Z reports higher scores in Brand Engagement (3.74 vs. 3.30, p &lt; 0.001) and Aesthetic Appeal (3.79 vs. 3.35, p = 0.003), suggesting a stronger response to visual storytelling, familiar IPs, and interactive experiences.<br>&nbsp;</p>
<p><b>Strategic Implication</b></p>
<p>Early Gen Z responds strongly to visual and sensory appeal, while deeper cultural meaning becomes increasingly important for sustained engagement across age groups.</p>
